&lt;p&gt;# Comments: 0&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50057256</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 14:51:07 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>Show HN: Baa – a menu bar app that frees RAM your AI agents forgot about</title><link>https://github.com/selviarora/baa</link><description>&lt;p&gt;i built this because my mac keeps running out of RAM every 2 hours and i typically get around it by closing random apps and hoping it will help. :')&lt;p&gt;baa sits in the menu bar and:&lt;p&gt;- finds stuff still eating memory after its app or terminal closed, or that ai agents started and forgot (dev servers, headless browsers)&lt;p&gt;- shows how much you'd get back and frees it in one click&lt;p&gt;- warns you a few minutes before you run out&lt;p&gt;- also finds dev junk on your disk (old builds, package caches etc.)&lt;p&gt;open source and nothing leaves your machine. would love feedback!&lt;p&gt;baa would've cleared ~50gb on my mac :)&lt;/p&gt;
